      "rule": "S5",
      "owner": "_FileHandler.handleError",
      "reason": "The class directly subclasses logging.FileHandler. handleError is the required standard-library callback invoked by emit after a write failure; renaming it would restore stderr tracebacks and lose failed_writes accounting. A real handler write failure preserves the existing file, increments once, emits no stderr, and a subsequent write succeeds.",
